# Understanding Chunks

Prometheus does not store every metric separately.

Instead, it groups consecutive samples together.

Example:

| Time  | CPU |
| ----- | --- |
| 10:00 | 20  |
| 10:15 | 25  |
| 10:30 | 30  |
| 10:45 | 40  |

Stored internally as:

```text
Chunk #1

20
25
30
40
```

A Chunk is simply:

```text
A small block containing consecutive metric samples.
```

Benefits:

* Faster writes
* Better compression
* Efficient storage

---

# Understanding Index

Prometheus may contain millions of metrics.

Without an index, searching would be slow.

Example:

```text
CPU Metrics
Memory Metrics
Disk Metrics
Network Metrics
```

Prometheus maintains an index:

```text
CPU --> Location A
Memory --> Location B
Disk --> Location C
```

When Grafana requests CPU data:

```text
Grafana --> Prometheus
```

Prometheus checks the index and immediately finds the correct data.

Think of the index as:

```text
Table of Contents in a book
```

